    "https://secure4.saashr.com/ta/6153588.careers?ShowJob=1040454912": {
      "title": "6153588:Career Search",
      "description": "6153588:Career Search Skip to Main Content Log in Adjunct Instructor of Health and Medicine Show All Jobs Apply Show Map Location 100 N East Ave,\n    \n                      Waukesha, WI, 53186,\n                      United States Job Category Health and Medicine, Adjunct Relocation Expense Covered No Employee Type Adjunct Faculty Manage Others No Description Adjunct Instructor of Anatomy and Physiology Starting date: Fall 2026 Carroll University seeks to hire an Adjunct Instru ctor of Anatomy and Physiology for the Fall 2026 Course: ANP130L | Introduction to Human Anatomy and Physiology I Laboratory In this laboratory support class students explore the unifying concepts of anatomy and physiology required for understanding the human body as a structural and functional unit. This course emphasizes the mechanisms that underlie the normal functions of cells, tissues, organs, and organ systems. This course includes the study of basic biochemistry, cell biology, histology, and the integumentary, skeletal, muscular, nervous, and endocrine systems. Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in related discipline.  Additional graduate work required. ANP130L      F Day/Time: T, 9:20AM- 11:50AM, On Campus ANP130L      O Day/Time: R, 9:20AM- 11:50AM, On Campus The Program: The Anatomy and Physiology courses serve several disciplines including athletic training, biology, exercise science, nursing, physical and health education, pre-physical therapy, public health, and sports administration. The curriculum is designed to provide students an introductory and/or advanced knowledge of anatomy and physiology. The courses provide a foundation for those who wish to pursue graduate studies or professional health careers. The College: The College of Health Sciences offers undergraduate and graduate programs through seven departments: Athletic Training, Human Movement Sciences, Nursing, Occupational Therapy, Physical Therapy, Physician Assistant Studies, and Public Health. The mission of the College of Health Sciences is to educate students to be innovative professionals who collaborate to serve the health needs of their communities. The College of Health Sciences currently accounts for ~60% of University enrollment. A dynamic and growing entity, College wide foci include interprofessional education and practice, the integrated approach to health, innovative learning and healthcare technologies, community partnerships and service to medically underserved populations. To support these initiatives the University has recently renovated a medical arts building to house and support its service learning and Community Health Service programs and partnered with the Waukesha Free Clinic at Carroll University. The College supports the interdisciplinary nature of health science education and has received federal and private foundation grant awards to support these, as well as program specific initiatives. Carroll University: Founded in 1846, Carroll University is an independent, co-educational comprehensive university grounded in the liberal arts tradition. T he Pioneer Core general education curriculum has a strong emphasis on developing intercultural awareness, including cross-cultural immersion experiences. Carroll University is located in suburban Waukesha, 16 miles west of Milwaukee and 60 miles east of Madison. The University serves approximately 3521 students. The University though intentionally ecumenical and non- sectarian in approach, is related to the Presbyterian Church, USA. Candidates must be willing and able to support and advance the University mission . Application: Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. As part of your application, please submit a cover letter, CV and examples of teaching effectiveness. If you have past course evaluations, please submit several that demonstrate your teaching effectiveness. Carroll University is an Equal-Opportunity Employer Requirements As part of your application, please submit  a cover letter, CV and examples of teaching effectiveness. If you have past course evaluations, please submit several that demonstrate your teaching effectiveness. In lieu of course evaluations, a letter from your current supervisor attesting to your skills in the classroom environment. Carroll University makes employment opportunities available to qualified individuals whose skills and experience make them suitable candidates for placement. Candidates must be willing and able to support and advance the University mission. Carroll University does not discriminate in any manner contrary to law or justice on the basis of race, color, sex, age, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability or veteran's status in administration of programs or in the employment of faculty and staff. The employment opportunities list is updated periodically based on openings. Applications will be accepted only for vacancies currently listed. All inquiries will be kept strictly confidential."
    },
    "https://secure4.saashr.com/ta/6153588.careers?ShowJob=1040451910": {
      "title": "6153588:Career Search",
      "description": "6153588:Career Search Skip to Main Content Log in Dean - Sullivan School of Business, Engineering & Technology Show All Jobs Apply Show Map Location 100 N East Ave,\n    \n                      Waukesha, WI, 53186,\n                      United States Job Category School of Business, Staff Employee Type Administrative Staff Description Description:      At Carroll University, we are committed to identifying and employing strategies to support our goal to be and remain a socially just organization. Rooted in the Presbyterian (U.S.A.) heritage, we respect all aspects of diversity, embrace the practice of equity, expect inclusion, and embrace belonging throughout our community. Therefore, we seek applicants who can demonstrate their understanding of justice and who can inspire our increasingly diverse student population. The Dean of The Sullivan School of Business, Engineering and Technology (SSBET) serves as the chief academic and administrative officer of the school and provides strategic leadership to advance its mission, enrollment, reputation, and impact. The Dean is responsible for academic quality, faculty leadership, financial stewardship, external partnerships, fundraising, accreditation oversight, and long-range planning. The Dean represents the school to university leadership, alumni, donors, business and industry partners, and the broader community while fostering an innovative, student-centered culture that prepares graduates for successful careers and leadership. Responsibilities: •    Create a supportive teaching and learning environment for students, faculty, and staff. •    Facilitate the annual strategic planning and goal setting process for the SSBET in conjunction with Academic Affairs’ strategic initiatives and Carroll University’s mission, ethos, and strategic plan. •    Engage in successful revenue generation, donor cultivation, and school-wide advancement and marketing in partnership with Institutional Advancement. •    Maintain productive relationships with national and international business communities. •    Lead all external partnerships, including the school’s advisory board. •    Ensure the expansion and development of market-driven global programs across the school. •    Represent the SSBET to the Deans’ Council, Board of Trustees, university community, and external audiences to communicate the school’s capabilities, accomplishments, impact, and aspirations. •    Ensure the school meets or exceeds all accreditation requirements. •    Serve as the SSBET primary representative, spokesperson, and advocate in the school’s student recruitment, retention, and reputation management efforts. •    Recruit, develop, evaluate, and lead the chairs, faculty and staff in the SSBET in a manner that inspires individuals and teams to perform at their best. •    Develop budgets, staffing plans, and collaborative allocation of scarce resources with chairs and departmental faculty. •    Complete annual performance evaluation of chairs, administrators, and staff; collaborating with chairs on performance evaluation of faculty. •    Make recommendations for promotion, tenure and sabbaticals to the relevant faculty governance committees. •    Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications: Education and Experience: •    Doctorate or terminal degree preferred, preferably in a discipline within the school •    20+ years of successful experience in higher education and/or business, with evidence of increased levels of responsibilities of leadership •    An understanding of the business of private higher education •    A strong record of partnerships with external stakeholders •    Experience with change management Human Relations Skills: •    A record of progressive and proven leadership experience •    A strong record of success in attaining external funding through gifts, grants, and partnerships •    Ability to work effectively with people regardless of their age, gender, race, sexual orientation, ethnicity, religion, ability, socio-economic background, or job type. •    Evidence of a collaborative leadership and management style that advances goals and programs, evokes trust, and effectively engages the talents, strengths, and experiences of faculty, staff, alumni, and donors •    Outstanding communication skills •    Highly developed relationship-building skills and evidence of strong ties to regional businesses and other stakeholders •    Candidates must be willing and able to support and advance the University Mission Compliance: •    Employees may be required to report violations of law under Title IX and the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act). If this position is identified a Campus Security Authority (Clery Act), you will be notified and provided resources for reporting. The Clery Act requires all prospective employees be notified of the availability of the Annual Security and Fire Safety report. You may access the most recent report here or obtain a copy at the Department of Public Safety, at 239 North East Ave, Waukesha, WI 53186 Campus Security Authority Responsibilities: This position is designated as a Campus Security Authority in accordance with the Clery Act. This position will be required to report Clery crimes to Public Safety and complete annual training about reporting responsibilities. Requirements Please submit a cover letter and resume for this position along with this electronic application. Carroll University makes employment opportunities available to qualified individuals whose skills and experience make them suitable candidates for placement. Candidates must be willing and able to support and advance the University mission. Carroll University does not discriminate in any manner contrary to law or justice on the basis of race, color, sex, age, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability or veteran's status in administration of programs or in the employment of faculty and staff. The employment opportunities list is updated periodically based on openings. Applications will be accepted only for vacancies currently listed. All inquiries will be kept strictly confidential."
    },
    "https://secure4.saashr.com/ta/6153588.careers?ShowJob=1023737812": {
      "title": "6153588:Career Search",
      "description": "6153588:Career Search Skip to Main Content Log in Assistant eSports Coach Show All Jobs Apply Show Map Location 100 N EAST AVE,\n    \n                      WAUKESHA, WI, 53186,\n                      United States Job Category Rec Sports, Staff Employee Type Part-Time Coach Description Description:     At Carroll University, we are committed to identifying and employing strategies to support our goal to be and remain a socially just organization. Rooted in the Presbyterian (U.S.A.) heritage, we respect all aspects of diversity, embrace the practice of equity, expect inclusion, and embrace belonging throughout our community. Therefore, we seek applicants who can demonstrate their understanding of justice and who can inspire our increasingly diverse student population. This position will assist the head coach in recruiting and coaching duties. The successful coach will be directly involved in recruiting student-players, coaching in-person and online, and building the program identity. This position reports to the Head eSports Coach. The preferred candidate will have the ability to work a flexible schedule, including evenings and weekends. Travel for team tournaments and recruiting may be required. Responsibilities: Assistant the Head Coach to coach and instruct activities during practice and competition Understand and comply with all rules and regulations set forth by Carroll University and eSports competitions Act as a professional and positive representative of the Carroll University Educational Experience. Provide guidance and input on games selected for varsity competition To lead dedicated team practice and games in person. Developing and employing structured practices. Provide care and oversight of equipment and facility Assist with team travel when necessary; including but not limited to driving athletes to competition. Recruit and retain students for the Esports program Support and work camps, clinics and promotional events Perform other duties as assigned Qualifications: Education and/or Experience: Associates degree from an accredited college or university preferred. One-year competitive eSports experience involving multiplayer online video games with team-based elements preferred Significant knowledge of one or more of the following games preferred: League of Legends, Overwatch, Valorant, Rocket League, Call of Duty, and/or Smash Bros. Strong relationship-building skills Effective written and oral communication skills, including public speaking Ability to work with a diverse community of students, faculty, administrators and professional colleagues Valid driver’s license and ability to travel required Candidates must be willing and able to support and advance the University mission. Competitive Gaming/Computer Skills: Understanding of computer hardware and software needs related to competitive Esports while collaborating with the Office of Information Technology (OIT). Ability to operate gaming PC and console equipment to meet the needs of an Esports program competing in both formats. Human Relations Skills: •    Excellent oral and written communication skills •    Positive attitude towards the University and its intercollegiate programs is essential •    Ability to conduct self in a productive, professional manner at all times •    Candidates must be willing and able to support and advance the University Mission. Compliance: •    Employees may be required to report violations of law under Title IX and the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act). If this position is identified a Campus Security Authority (Clery Act), you will be notified and provided resources for reporting. The Clery Act requires all prospective employees be notified of the availability of the Annual Security and Fire Safety report. You may access the most recent report here or obtain a copy at the Department of Public Safety, at 239 North East Ave, Waukesha, WI 53186 Campus Security Authority Responsibilities: This position is designated as a Campus Security Authority in accordance with the Clery Act. This position will be required to report Clery crimes to Public Safety and complete annual training about reporting responsibilities. Requirements Please submit a cover letter and resume for this position along with this electronic application. Carroll University makes employment opportunities available to qualified individuals whose skills and experience make them suitable candidates for placement. Candidates must be willing and able to support and advance the University mission. Carroll University does not discriminate in any manner contrary to law or justice on the basis of race, color, sex, age, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability or veteran's status in administration of programs or in the employment of faculty and staff. The employment opportunities list is updated periodically based on openings. Applications will be accepted only for vacancies currently listed. All inquiries will be kept strictly confidential."
