    "https://secure4.saashr.com/ta/6153588.careers?ShowJob=1023725893": {
      "title": "6153588:Career Search",
      "description": "6153588:Career Search Skip to Main Content Log in Director of Business Technology Solutions Show All Jobs Apply Show Map Location 100 N East Ave,\n    \n                      Waukesha, WI, 53186,\n                      United States Job Category Information Technology, Staff Employee Type Administrative Staff Required Degree 4 Year Degree Manage Others Yes Minimum Experience 10 Years Description At Carroll University, we are committed to identifying and employing strategies to support our goal to be and remain a socially just organization. Rooted in the Presbyterian (U.S.A.) heritage, we respect all aspects of diversity, embrace the practice of equity, expect inclusion, and embrace belonging throughout our community. Therefore, we seek applicants who can demonstrate their understanding of justice and who can inspire our increasingly diverse student population. The Director of Business Technology Solutions provides strategic leadership for aligning technology solutions, business processes, and data with Carroll University’s institutional priorities. This role leads Business Analysis, Application Development, Project Delivery, Enterprise Applications, and Data & Analytics, partnering across the University to improve processes, deliver effective solutions, and advance strategic initiatives. Responsibilities: Provide strategic leadership for Business Technology Solutions, ensuring technology initiatives, business processes, data, and solutions align with University priorities and goals. Lead and develop teams responsible for Business Analysis, Application Development, Project Delivery, Enterprise Applications, and Data & Analytics, fostering collaboration, accountability, and continuous improvement. Partner with University leaders and campus stakeholders to understand business needs, identify opportunities, and translate strategic and operational priorities into effective technology solutions. Lead business process analysis and improvement efforts, evaluating people, process, data, and technology to improve efficiency, effectiveness, and the campus experience. Provide thought leadership on technology, AI, emerging technologies, and innovative solutions that support institutional transformation and strategic objectives. Oversee the evaluation, selection, implementation, integration, and optimization of enterprise applications and technology solutions. Establish and promote standards, governance, and best practices for solution delivery, application development, business analysis, data, and project execution. Oversee the effectiveness and continued evolution of enterprise applications, integrations, and technology solutions, identifying opportunities to improve, modernize, consolidate, or replace existing capabilities. Partner with technical and functional teams, vendors, and other stakeholders to deliver secure, scalable, and sustainable solutions. Provide leadership for data and analytics capabilities that strengthen data accessibility, governance, reporting, and data-informed decision-making across the University. Oversee the prioritization and delivery of technology initiatives, balancing institutional priorities, business value, resource capacity, risk, and dependencies. Build strong relationships across the University and serve as a trusted technology partner and advisor to campus leadership and stakeholders. Collaborate with OIT Leadership team to review and maintain strategic roadmaps for business technology capabilities, enterprise systems, and data. Perform additional duties as required. Qualifications: Education and/or Experience: Bachelor’s degree in information technology, Information Systems, Computer Science, Business, or a related field required; equivalent combination of education and relevant professional experience may be considered. Minimum of ten years of progressively responsible experience in information technology, business technology, enterprise applications, solution delivery, or a related field. Minimum of five years of leadership experience managing and developing technology professionals and/or multidisciplinary technology teams. Demonstrated experience leading complex technology initiatives and delivering enterprise solutions that support organizational strategy and business needs. Experience partnering with business and organizational leaders to evaluate processes, identify opportunities, define requirements, and translate business needs into effective technology solutions. Strong understanding of enterprise applications, application development and integration, data and analytics, project delivery methodologies, and modern technology architectures. Experience evaluating, selecting, implementing, integrating, and optimizing enterprise technology solutions and vendor-provided platforms. Experience developing strong partnerships with technical teams, business stakeholders, vendors, and organizational leadership. Knowledge of emerging technologies, including artificial intelligence, automation, cloud technologies, and evolving approaches to enterprise technology and solution delivery. Higher education experience preferred but not required. Technical Skills: Strong understanding of enterprise technology ecosystems, including ERP and other enterprise applications, application development, systems integration, data and analytics, and cloud-based technologies. Conceptual knowledge of modern application and data architecture, including APIs and integrations, relational databases, data management, reporting and analytics technologies, data governance, and identity and access management. Knowledge in software development lifecycle (SDLC), application lifecycle management, and solution delivery methodologies. (Agile, Waterfall, Hybrid) Understanding artificial intelligence, automation, and emerging technologies, with the ability to evaluate their potential business value, risks, and appropriate application. Experience using project management software. Human Relations Skills: Exceptional communication, analytical, interpersonal, and relationship-building skills, with the ability to effectively engage technical and non-technical audiences at all levels of the University. Ability to work effectively with people regardless of their age, gender, race, sexual orientation, ethnicity, religion, ability, socio-economic background or job type. Demonstrated leadership experience building, motivating, developing, and empowering high-performing teams while fostering accountability, collaboration, and professional growth. Ability to build trusted partnerships, influence decision-making, navigate differing perspectives, and develop consensus across diverse stakeholder groups. Demonstrated ability to lead teams and stakeholders through organizational, process, and technology change while encouraging innovation, adaptability, and continuous improvement. Strong leadership experience in building, motivating, developing and managing employees. Ability to develop, nurture and encourage staff to embrace change and move the institution forward. Candidates must be willing and able to support and advance the University mission. Compliance: Employees may be required to report violations of law under Title IX and the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act). If this position is identified a Campus Security Authority (Clery Act), you will be notified and provided resources for reporting. The Clery Act requires all prospective employees be notified of the availability of the Annual Security and Fire Safety report. You may access the most recent report here or obtain a copy at the Department of Public Safety, at 239 North East Ave, Waukesha, WI 53186 Requirements Please submit a cover letter and resume for this position along with this electronic application. Carroll University makes employment opportunities available to qualified individuals whose skills and experience make them suitable candidates for placement. Candidates must be willing and able to support and advance the University mission. Carroll University does not discriminate in any manner contrary to law or justice on the basis of race, color, sex, age, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability or veteran's status in administration of programs or in the employment of faculty and staff. The employment opportunities list is updated periodically based on openings. Applications will be accepted only for vacancies currently listed. All inquiries will be kept strictly confidential."
    },
    "https://secure4.saashr.com/ta/6153588.careers?ShowJob=1023725892": {
      "title": "6153588:Career Search",
      "description": "6153588:Career Search Skip to Main Content Log in Sr. Data Analyst Show All Jobs Apply Show Map Location 100 N East Ave,\n    \n                      Waukesha, WI, 53186,\n                      United States Job Category Information Technology Services, Staff Employee Type Administrative Staff Required Degree 4 Year Degree Manage Others No Minimum Experience 5 Years Description At Carroll University, we are committed to identifying and employing strategies to support our goal to be and remain a socially just organization. Rooted in the Presbyterian (U.S.A.) heritage, we respect all aspects of diversity, embrace the practice of equity, expect inclusion, and embrace belonging throughout our community. Therefore, we seek applicants who can demonstrate their understanding of justice and who can inspire our increasingly diverse student population. The Senior Data Analyst is a strategic and technical role within Information Technology responsible for advancing the institution’s data analytics, reporting, and decision-support capabilities. This position partners closely with academic and administrative departments to analyze data, develop actionable insights, improve data quality, and support data-informed decision-making across the institution. The Senior Data Analyst designs and develops enterprise reporting solutions, dashboards, data models, and analytics frameworks while helping establish data governance standards and best practices. This role serves as a bridge between business stakeholders and technical teams to ensure institutional data is accurate, accessible, secure, and aligned with strategic goals. The position requires strong analytical, communication, and problem-solving skills, along with experience working with ERP systems, data visualization tools, SQL, and modern analytics platforms in a collaborative higher education environment. Responsibilities : Design, develop, and maintain enterprise dashboards, reports, and data visualizations for academic and administrative departments. Translate complex business requirements into meaningful analytics and reporting solutions. Support institutional data governance initiatives, including data quality, integrity, stewardship, and standardization efforts. Partner with stakeholders to establish consistent reporting definitions, business rules, and data standards. Assist in maintaining enterprise data models, data dictionaries, and metadata documentation. Promote responsible and secure use of institutional data in alignment with compliance and privacy requirements. Assist departments seeking to improve operational effectiveness through data insights. Assist with prioritizing analytics initiatives. Work with enterprise systems including ERP/SIS, CRM, HRIS, LMS, and other institutional applications to support data integration and reporting. Develop and optimize SQL queries, data pipelines, and automated reporting processes. Support analytics and business intelligence platforms such as Power BI, or similar tools. Assist in evaluating emerging analytics, AI, and data technologies that improve institutional effectiveness. Identify opportunities to improve reporting efficiency, automation, and data accessibility. Participate in cross-functional IT and institutional projects related to data, reporting, and process improvement. Complete other duties as assigned. Qualifications : Education and/or Experience: · Bachelor’s degree in Information Systems, Computer Science, Data Analytics, Business, Mathematics, Statistics, or related field. · 5+ years of experience in data analytics, business intelligence, institutional research, or related analytics roles. · Experience working in higher education environments, desired. · Strong experience with SQL and relational databases. · Strong analytical, problem-solving, and communication skills. · Ability to explain technical concepts and analytics insights to non-technical audiences. · Experience supporting institutional effectiveness, enrollment analytics, student success, or operational reporting initiatives. Technical Skills: · Experience developing dashboards and reports using Power BI, Tableau, or similar BI tools. · Experience working with enterprise applications such as ERP, SIS, CRM, or HRIS systems. · Familiarity with Ellucian, Anthology, Workday, Salesforce, or similar higher education platforms. · Experience with data warehousing, ETL/integration processes, or cloud analytics platforms. · Knowledge of data governance, compliance, and privacy practices. · Exposure to predictive analytics, AI, or machine learning concepts. Human Relations Skills: · Ability to work effectively with people regardless of their age, gender, race, sexual orientation, ethnicity, religion, ability, socio-economic background, or job type. · Effective interpersonal and communication skills with the ability to collaborate across teams and contribute to problem-solving efforts. · Clear and professional written and verbal communication skills suited for both technical and non-technical audiences. · Strong commitment to delivering responsive and respectful customer service. · Ability to stay focused, organized, and productive when working under deadlines or during periods of high activity. · Adaptable and able to manage shifting priorities in a dynamic work environment. · Skilled in managing multiple assignments and projects simultaneously with minimal oversight. · Equally comfortable working independently or as part of a collaborative team. · Demonstrated ability to build and maintain positive working relationships with a wide range of colleagues and stakeholders. · Candidates must be willing and able to support and advance the University mission . Compliance: · Employees may be required to report violations of law under Title IX and the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act). If this position is identified a Campus Security Authority (Clery Act), you will be notified and provided resources for reporting. The Clery Act requires all prospective employees be notified of the availability of the Annual Security and Fire Safety report. You may access the most recent report here or obtain a copy at the Department of Public Safety, at 239 North East Ave., Waukesha, WI 5318 This position has a hybrid work arrangement - 3 days in office, 2 days remote. Requirements Please submit a cover letter and resume for this position along with this electronic application. Carroll University makes employment opportunities available to qualified individuals whose skills and experience make them suitable candidates for placement. Candidates must be willing and able to support and advance the University mission. Carroll University does not discriminate in any manner contrary to law or justice on the basis of race, color, sex, age, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability or veteran's status in administration of programs or in the employment of faculty and staff. The employment opportunities list is updated periodically based on openings. Applications will be accepted only for vacancies currently listed. All inquiries will be kept strictly confidential."
    },
    "https://secure4.saashr.com/ta/6153588.careers?ShowJob=1023724992": {
      "title": "6153588:Career Search",
      "description": "6153588:Career Search Skip to Main Content Log in Assistant Men's Lacrosse Coach Show All Jobs Apply Show Map Location 100 N East Ave,\n    \n                      Waukesha, WI, 53186,\n                      United States Job Category Athletics Employee Type Part-Time Coach Required Degree NONE Manage Others No Minimum Experience 1 Year Maximum Experience 15 Years Description Description: At Carroll University, we are committed to identifying and employing strategies to support our goal to be and remain a socially just organization. Rooted in the Presbyterian (U.S.A.) heritage, we respect all aspects of diversity, embrace the practice of equity, expect inclusion, and embrace belonging throughout our community. Therefore, we seek applicants who can demonstrate their understanding of justice and who can inspire our increasingly diverse student population . The Assistant Coach is responsible for assisting the Head Coach in the development and maintenance of an effective and competitive NCAA Division III Men’s Lacrosse program at Carroll University.  Teaching will include instruction of the skills and strategies necessary for the student-athlete to become competitive and successful in this sport. The recruitment and retention of quality student-athletes in this program will be integral to this position.  The Assistant Coach will also be expected to teach and demonstrate the ability to promote the physical, intellectual and social growth of student-athletes. The Assistant Coach is also responsible for assisting the Head Coach in their assigned responsibilities and in the direction of all aspects of their assigned sport program Responsibilities: Coaching: Understand and comply with all rules and guidelines set forth b y the NCAA Division III , Carroll University, CCIW (College Conference of Illinois and Wisconsin), and Carroll University Athletics. Understand and compl y with the NCAA and Carroll University philosophy and mission. Act as a professional and positive representative of the Carroll University Educational Experience. Serve as a teacher, counselor, and role model so that student athletes will improve upon their physical, intellectual, and social behaviors. Maximize the physical talent of the team through quality teaching and coaching, and the promotion of teamwork. Assist the Head Coach in planning, organizing and administering all practice sessions. Assist in recruitment of student athletes while work ing through the Head Coach with the Office of Admission to maximize enrollment. Retain student athletes at Carroll University and within the team. Assist in m aintain ing , manag ing and updat ing equipment inventories. Teach the skills and strategies necessary for the student-athletes’ success in this sport. Assist with the management and maintenance of all game and practice facilities used by the team. Assist in the teaching and coaching of a sub-varsity team. Participate in team and departmental camps/clinics, community service projects, fundraising activities, and alumni events whenever possible. Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications: Education and/or Experience: Bachelor’s degree required Expertise in the sport on intercollegiate level (desired) Previous playing or coaching experience (desired) Teaching, and/or other certifications required for this position, and/or previous teaching experience Human Relations Skills: Ability to function effectively as a team player Excellent oral and written communication skills Sensitivity to the needs of student -athlete s and an understanding of their overall educational goals as well as the academic mission of the University Positive attitude towards the University and its intercollegiate programs is essential Ability to conduct self in a productive, professional manner at all times Candidates must be willing and able to support and advance the University mission . Ability to work effectively with people regardless of their age, gender, race, sexual orientation, ethnicity, religion, ability, socio-economic background, or job type. Special Requirements: Must have valid motor vehicle license and be insurable under the University’s insurance plan. Compliance: Employees may be required to report violations of law under Title IX and the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act). If this position is identified a Campus Security Authority (Clery Act), you will be notified and provided resources for reporting. The Clery Act requires all prospective employees be notified of the availability of the Annual Security and Fire Safety report. You may access the most recent report here or obtain a copy at the Department of Public Safety, at 208 Wright St., Waukesha, WI 53186. Campus Security Authority Responsibilities This position is designated as a Campus Security Authority in accordance with the Clery Act. This position will be required to report Clery crimes to Public Safety and complete annual training about reporting responsibilities."
    },
